  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "SQL injection (SQLi) is a type of security vulnerability that allows an
    attacker to interfere with the queries a web application makes to its database.
    It happens when user input is not properly sanitized and is directly included
    in SQL statements. By injecting malicious SQL code (like ' OR '1'='1), an attacker
    can manipulate the query to bypass login forms, extract sensitive data, modify
    or delete database entries, or even gain full control of the database. \n\nSQL
    injection is one of the most common and dangerous web vulnerabilities and is
    preventable by using secure coding practices like prepared statements and input
    validation."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
